## Original Content
The US threatened Iran with what it called "the greatest financial offensive ever marshalled" as it prepared to ​roll out economic sanctions on Monday that target Iran's trade partners.

## Summary
The US has vowed to impose significant economic sanctions on Iran, referring to it as an 'economic D-Day', in response to Iran's threat to halt Gulf oil exports. The sanctions are targeted at Iran's trade partners and are described by the US as the greatest financial offensive ever marshalled.

## Key Points
- The US is preparing to roll out economic sanctions on Iran.
- The sanctions specifically target Iran's trade partners.
- Iran has threatened to halt Gulf oil exports as a countermeasure.
- The US has characterized the sanctions as a major financial offensive.


